course: dictionary
lesson: 7591
title: Prickle: sharp points and tingly feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A prickle is a small, sharp point, like the ones on a hedgehog, a holly leaf or a bramble. Prickle can also be a feeling: a tingling or stinging on your skin.
explain: Prickle can be a verb too, so it can show an action. «The wool prickled my neck.» Try the meaning in the sentence: "The wool gave my neck a stinging, tingling feeling" makes sense, so that is the meaning here.
explain: Your skin can prickle when you feel fear or excitement. In a story, «the hairs on the back of her neck prickled» tells you the character senses danger, even though the author does not say she is scared. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
fact: A prickle is a small sharp point on a plant or an animal.
fact: «His paw fills with prickles» means his paw is full of sharp points.
fact: «Prickle» as a verb means to give a stinging or tingling feeling, as in «the wool prickled my neck».
fact: «A prickle of fear» means a sudden tingling feeling of being scared.
fact: «Prickle with tears» means your eyes sting as if you are about to cry.
exercise: «His paw fills with prickles, and Hedgehog flies off into the dark bushes.» What are the prickles? | Soft, warm blankets | Tiny drops of rain | *Small sharp points | Bright lights
exercise: «The wool prickled my neck.» What does prickled mean here? | A soft, gentle stroke | *A stinging, tingling feeling | A loud noise | Wet and cold
exercise: In a story, the hairs on her neck prickled. What is the author telling us? | She is bored of school | *She senses danger | She is very sleepy | She has just had a haircut
test: Which of these has prickles? | Feather | Glass window | Silk scarf | *Holly leaf
test: «A prickle of fear» means what? | A cold drink on a hot day | *A sudden tingling feeling of being scared | A sharp bite from a dog | A short, quiet song
exam: «Her eyes began to prickle with tears.» What does prickle mean here? | Dry out in the sun | *Sting, as if she is about to cry | Close tightly shut | Turn red from laughing
